<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n71834" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ξῠρόν</span></b> , τό, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>razor,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>El.</u>
				241
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ec.</u>
				65
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Th.</u>
				219
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Al.</u>
				411
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Art.</u>
				29
			</span></i>, etc.: prov., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ ξυροῦ ἵσταται
				ἀκμῆς . . , ὄλεθρος ἠὲ βιῶναι</span> death or life is
			balanced on a <i>razor's</i> edge, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				10.173
			</span></i> : freq. in later authors, to express a delicately balanced
				like lihood of failure or success, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκμᾶς ἑστακυῖαν ἐπὶ ξυροῦ Ἑλλάδα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Simon.
					97
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ ξ. γὰρ ἀκμῆς ἔχεται ἡμῖν τὰ
					πρήγματα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					6.11
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κίνδυνος ἐπὶ ξ. ἵσταται ἀκμῆς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thgn.
					557
				</span></i>
			 ; 
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βεβὼς . . ἐπὶ ξ. τύχης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ant.</u>
					996
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔβητ᾽ ἐπὶ ξ.</span> ; <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>HF</u>
				630
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ ξ. εἶναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					22.6
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὶ ξ. ἑστηκέναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>JTr.</u>
					3
				</span></i>
			.</div>
